  "summary_md": "Demand remains subdued across furnishings, pressured by housing weakness and discretionary pullbacks. Tariff-related effects ripple through the batch: COOK and HBB saw margin lifts from refunds or exclusions, FLXS passed surcharges on, and ATER’s ultimate upside hinges on a contingent value right for invalidated 2025 duties. Strategic reshaping dominates the morning: ATER exited operations entirely, becoming a cash-distribution shell, while SNBR filed Chapter 11, wiping out equity. AMWD’s pending MasterBrand acquisition keeps M&A in focus. Speculative pivots outside core furniture appear at MWYN and XWIN, both chasing AI and data-center narratives, and NCL navigates yield headwinds alongside an activist pact. Margin resilience at COOK and FLXS, plus insider buying at VIRC and EFOI, round out a group defined more by transformation and tactical repositioning than by a broad demand recovery.",
  "summary_date": "2026-06-16"
